From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Henk Wiedig <henk@wiedig.de>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 21:54:24 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] drm/artosyn: Lontium LT9611EX DSI to HDMI bridge (BetaFPV
 P1 HD VRX)

The P1 HD VRX is the VR04 goggles' board with a Lontium LT9611EX where the
panel is. The chip's own firmware measures the DSI video and drives the
matching HDMI mode; the host resets it and, over I2C (0x41, page 0xE0
mailbox), switches the output on/off and HDMI/DVI and reads HPD and EDID.
All after stock's libpn_lt9611ex.so (P1_GND 2.1.4): reset GPIO 107 active
low (20 ms high, 100 ms low, high, 500 ms), chip ID at page 0xE1, the
mailbox handshake, the EDID by RH2: (length) and RH3: + n (32-byte chunks).

The connector lists the sink's modes from its EDID (re-read at every probe)
as far as the chain drives them, the sink's preferred one marked, so
userspace picks a mode as on any HDMI output. The SoC sends stock's
DSI-side timing for the chosen HDMI mode - the same active size and frame
rate with longer horizontal blanking, from libpn_lt9611ex.so's attrs for
1080p60/50/30 and 720p60/50 - which atomic_check puts into the adjusted mode
for artosyn_vo/artosyn_dsi (artosyn,timing-from-mode). A mode is listed when
the "pixel" clock reaches its DSI-side rate (clk_round_rate); with today's
CGU driver (+-5 percent around the boot rate) that is 1080p60. Without an
EDID the list is the table's CEA modes the clock reaches, 1080p60 preferred;
when the sink's preferred mode is not drivable, the first drivable one in
the table's order becomes it.

Stock's VRX 2.0.8 opened a disabled I2C bus, so the chip also runs without
I2C: when it does not answer, the driver warns and drives the DSI side
alone. It makes a DSI device on the host (4 lanes RGB888 video, as the
panel) and, since artosyn_vo attaches the chain without NO_CONNECTOR, the
HDMI-A connector, always connected (the chip follows the sink's hot plug).

sysfs chip_id, i2c_ok, hpd, mailbox and reset and the module options
skip_i2c, use_edid, hdmi_mode, dsi_mode and reset_ms are there for bring-up
without the unit at hand.
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/artosyn/Kconfig            |  13 +
 drivers/gpu/drm/artosyn/Makefile           |   1 +
 drivers/gpu/drm/artosyn/lontium-lt9611ex.c | 820 +++++++++++++++++++++
 3 files changed, 834 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 drivers/gpu/drm/artosyn/lontium-lt9611ex.c

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/artosyn/Kconfig b/drivers/gpu/drm/artosyn/Kconfig
