--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/artosyn/Kconfig
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/artosyn/Kconfig
@@ -20,3 +20,16 @@ config DRM_ARTOSYN
 	  display controller (CRTC), the DesignWare MIPI-DSI host (via the mainline
 	  dw-mipi-dsi bridge), and the QY45043A0 1080p60 panel. See
 	  ../../../../../docs/display-backlight.md.
+
+config DRM_LONTIUM_LT9611EX
+	tristate "Lontium LT9611EX MIPI-DSI to HDMI bridge (BetaFPV P1 HD VRX)"
+	depends on DRM_ARTOSYN && I2C && OF
+	select DRM_KMS_HELPER
+	select DRM_MIPI_DSI
+	help
+	  The HDMI output of the BetaFPV P1 HD VRX: a Lontium LT9611EX on the
+	  Artosyn DSI host instead of the goggles' panel. The chip's own
+	  firmware detects the DSI video and drives HDMI; the driver resets
+	  it, makes the DSI device and the HDMI connector, and switches the
